    },
    {
      "id": "QtKldhkkkRM9aeMfCNJBL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 934.5903602538892,
      "y": 2617.2915897787634,
      "width": 1409.6326904296875,
      "height": 492.297849251353,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4x",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 424579097,
      "version": 1974,
      "versionNonce": 2111071865,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "JLSrRgNgVF2aG78maJeip",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1745250709728,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Courier sends location every 5 seconds (12 times per minute)\n2. Average courier work day: 4 hours\n3. Max regional couriers amount: 15M (based on the research data)\n4. Each courier sends daily: 4 * 60 * 5 = 1200 location updates\n5. In a region couriers work during 8:00-24:00. 16 working hours\n6. Maximum in a region daily: (15000000 * 1200) = 18B locations updates\n7. Assumed spike in delivery demand within time range 14:00 - 22:00. 80% of the deliveries occur within this time range (8h).\n8. Max region RPS: 18*0.8B/(8*3600) = 500K req/sec of location updates\n9. Active couriers per region: 15 000 000 * (4 + 4 + 4 + 4) = 240M pure,  500M with footprint\n10. History: 15M x 1200 updates per day x 16b update size x 2 footprint = ~600GB daily\n11. History can be sieved, assume 30% of the data will be stored after sieving: 200GB daily\n12. 365 * 200GB ~= 80TB per year in region\n13. Assumed each courier handles 15 deliveries per work day\n14. 15M * 15 * 0.8 / (8*3600) = 6250 = ~10k RPS for courier routes\n15. 15k managers per region (keeping the ratio from global estimations)\n16. Manager's client performs periodic pooling, once per 10 sec ~= 360 per hour during 8 working hours\n17. 15k * 360 * 8 / (8*3600) = 1.5k RPS",
      "fontSize": 23.166957611828376,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Courier sends location every 5 seconds (12 times per minute)\n2. Average courier work day: 4 hours\n3. Max regional couriers amount: 15M (based on the research data)\n4. Each courier sends daily: 4 * 60 * 5 = 1200 location updates\n5. In a region couriers work during 8:00-24:00. 16 working hours\n6. Maximum in a region daily: (15000000 * 1200) = 18B locations updates\n7. Assumed spike in delivery demand within time range 14:00 - 22:00. 80% of the deliveries occur within this time range (8h).\n8. Max region RPS: 18*0.8B/(8*3600) = 500K req/sec of location updates\n9. Active couriers per region: 15 000 000 * (4 + 4 + 4 + 4) = 240M pure,  500M with footprint\n10. History: 15M x 1200 updates per day x 16b update size x 2 footprint = ~600GB daily\n11. History can be sieved, assume 30% of the data will be stored after sieving: 200GB daily\n12. 365 * 200GB ~= 80TB per year in region\n13. Assumed each courier handles 15 deliveries per work day\n14. 15M * 15 * 0.8 / (8*3600) = 6250 = ~10k RPS for courier routes\n15. 15k managers per region (keeping the ratio from global estimations)\n16. Manager's client performs periodic pooling, once per 10 sec ~= 360 per hour during 8 working hours\n17. 15k * 360 * 8 / (8*3600) = 1.5k RPS",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
